==English==
{{was wotd|2007|August|19}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*dyew-}}
From {{uder|en|fr|déifier}}, from {{uder|en|la|deificāre}}, from {{m|la|deus||god}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdeɪ.ɪ.faɪ/|/ˈdiː.ɪ.faɪ/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdiː.ə.faɪ/|/ˈdeɪ.ə.faɪ/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-deify.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-deify-2.ogg|a=US}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[make]] into a [[god]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[treat]] as [[worthy]] of [[worship]]; to [[regard]] as a [[deity]].
#* {{quote-journal|en-GB|author=Eva Corlett|quotee=w:Shane Jones|title=New Zealand will not be ‘guilt-tripped’ over environment, resources minister says|work=The Guardian|date=2025-05-26|url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/26/new-zealand-resources-minister-shane-jones-mining-environment|issn=0261-3077|passage=“Those people who have sought to '''deify''' our wilderness … those days are over. We are not going to sit around and read poetry to rare lizards, whilst our current account deficit goes down the gurgler,” Jones said.}}

